From: dtg01100 <dtg01100@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux: enable hardware watchdog core and x86 server drivers

0007 builds on the 0006 kubenet patch (which already owns the last
lines of fdsdk-config.sh): reproduce the last two lines of 0006 as
context so the hunks apply in order, then add the watchdog core +
x86-specific drivers below.

WATCHDOG / WATCHDOG_CORE are built in so no module dependency stands
between a driver and the core.  /dev/watchdog (and /dev/watchdog0) only
appear once a driver registers the first watchdog device, so
RuntimeWatchdogSec= stays a no-op on a node with no bound driver.  The
PCI/platform drivers (i6300esb, iTCO_wdt, sp5100_tco) carry modaliases
and autoload on matching hardware; it87_wdt, w83627hf_wdt, ipmi_watchdog
and softdog have none and must be loaded explicitly (modules-load.d or
modprobe).  softdog is deliberately not autoloaded: it would claim
watchdog0 ahead of a real hardware driver.

The x86 drivers are wrapped in an `arch == x86_64` guard because
ITCO_WDT / I6300ESB_WDT / SP5100_TCO / W83627HF_WDT / IT87_WDT are
x86-only Kconfig symbols and FSDK's `module()` script appends the name
to expected-configs (an aarch64 kernel build would otherwise fail
"Missing WXYZ" at olddefconfig time).

The W83627HF_WDT driver covers NCT6775/6776/6779/6791/6792 Super-I/O
watchdogs; there is no NUVOTON_NCT6775_WDT symbol in
drivers/watchdog/Kconfig.

---
 files/linux/fdsdk-config.sh | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/files/linux/fdsdk-config.sh b/files/linux/fdsdk-config.sh
--- a/files/linux/fdsdk-config.sh
+++ b/files/linux/fdsdk-config.sh
@@ -2828,2 +2828,15 @@
 enable INET_DIAG_DESTROY
 module NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_NOTRACK
+enable WATCHDOG
+enable WATCHDOG_CORE
+module SOFT_WATCHDOG
+module IPMI_WATCHDOG
+case "$arch" in
+    x86_64)
+        module I6300ESB_WDT     # Intel 6300ESB PCI watchdog (older servers).
+        module ITCO_WDT         # Intel ICH/PCH TCO watchdog (most x86 boards).
+        module SP5100_TCO       # AMD SP5100/AM79C974 TCO watchdog (AMD servers).
+        module IT87_WDT         # IT87xx Super-I/O watchdog (older motherboards).
+        module W83627HF_WDT     # W83627HF + NCT6775/6776/6779/6791/6792 Super-I/O watchdog.
+        ;;
+esac
